//! heap — the kernel heap and wolf's allocator hook (px06, M-PX2's
//! third piece).
//!
//! On `x86_64-unknown-none` wolf's `List`, `Map`, string interpolation,
//! capturing closures and `region` allocate through two functions the
//! program supplies (wolf-lang kw12, spec/04 `[abi.target.none.alloc]`):
//! `wolf_alloc(size, align) -> *u8` and `wolf_free(p, size, align)`.
//! This module is that pair, written in wolf, over px02's frames and
//! px03's paging. The runtime (`libwolf_rt_none.a`) asks for align 16
//! and sizes that are positive multiples of 16; it frees each block
//! exactly once, with its own size; a block it allocated outside every
//! `region` (the process root) it never frees. A null answer is
//! `alloc-contract` in the runtime, so this hook never returns one: out
//! of memory is a named panic here (the policy kw12 leaves to the hook).
//!
//! **Where.** PML4 slot 384, 0xffffc00000000000 (px03 and kw10 left
//! slots 256, 320, 352 and 511 taken). The slot's first 1 GiB holds the
//! heap's own books: one state page (the size classes' list heads) at
//! `META`, then a table of 64-byte page descriptors at `DESC`, one per
//! heap page, mapped a page at a time as the heap grows. The heap's
//! pages start at `BASE` (0xffffc04000000000) and grow upward from
//! there: `top` pages are mapped, each a `frames.alloc()` frame mapped
//! read-write no-execute by `paging.map` in the live structures. Pages
//! are never unmapped or handed back to `frames`: a page the heap has
//! once used stays the heap's, so no TLB entry ever goes stale (no
//! INVLPG to get right before a second CPU exists). The limit is
//! `MAX_PAGES` (128 MiB); past it, or when `frames` runs dry, the hook
//! panics `heap: out of memory`.
//!
//! **Two layers.**
//! - Pages. Runs of free heap pages sit on one doubly linked list in
//!   address order, found first-fit (the lowest run that fits); each run's first and last descriptors are its
//!   boundary tags (FREE_HEAD with the length, FREE_TAIL with the
//!   head), so a freed run merges with a free neighbour on either side
//!   in O(1). When no run fits, the heap grows at `top`, and a free run
//!   ending at `top` is extended rather than left behind.
//! - Blocks. A size up to 2048 bytes is rounded up to one of eight
//!   power-of-two classes, 16 to 2048 (or to its alignment, if larger).
//!   A class page is carved into equal blocks; its free blocks are
//!   threaded through their own first word on the class's list (the
//!   head in the state page); its descriptor keeps a 256-bit map of
//!   which blocks are allocated. A class page stays in its class: a
//!   freed block goes back to its class's list, never to the page
//!   layer. A larger size takes a whole run of pages, which goes back
//!   to the page layer on free.
//!
//! Why not one free list over all sizes: it cannot tell a double free,
//! or a free with the wrong size, without a header on every block; the
//! allocated map and the run tags catch both in O(1) with no header.
//! The runtime's sizes are few and power-of-two shaped (region chunks
//! of 1 KiB doubling to 1 MiB, 16- to 64-byte headers, the
//! interpolation buffer doubling from 64), so the classes waste little.
//! Why not a buddy system for pages: a region's 1 MiB + 16 chunk would
//! take 2 MiB.
//!
//! **Faults**, each `PANIC heap: <what> 0x<v>` (kernel/panic) and a
//! halt: a double free; a free outside the heap; a free whose size
//! does not match the block's; a free of an address that is not a
//! block's start; an alignment that is not a power of two or is above
//! 4096; a size that is not positive; out of memory; a call before
//! `start`. A page fault at a heap address names the heap
//! (kernel/interrupts).
//!
//! **The lock.** Since px07 kernel threads are preempted by the timer,
//! so two threads can both be inside the allocator: `alloc` and `free`
//! run under kernel/sync's heap lock (`sync.heap()`, a spinlock on
//! kw11's atomics that also clears IF, so on one CPU the holder is
//! never preempted and the lock never spins). wolf's freestanding
//! runtime takes no lock of its own (kw12); its region bump and its one
//! ambient-region slot are not the heap's to guard (see px06's notes
//! and wolf-lang's ambient-slot issue). No interrupt handler allocates:
//! one that did would spin forever on the lock its own CPU holds.
//!
//! State: the books are a `#[repr(c)] struct HeapState` at the start of
//! the heap's own state page, each field read and written as a `u64` at
//! its `offset_of` through `rd`/`wr` (module state is read only inside
//! `unsafe`, E1301, so one unsafe site serves them all, as in
//! kernel/frames); the one module `var` is `up`.
//!
//! wolf-lang#598 (native and release forward a module `var`'s value
//! across a call that writes it): audited 2026-10-06. The books are
//! reached through int-cast raw pointers, which both tiers reload after
//! a call that writes them (px06's probe: store or load, a call to a
//! writer, load again, all 99 on both tiers; only the module-`var`
//! shape answers stale). `up` is written only by `start` and no
//! function reads it, calls something that writes it, and reads it
//! again, so no site needs a reload. tests/mpx2-heap H10 is the
//! witness: `up` and the books read on either side of a writing call.
//!
//! The author's own design. The paging facts are px03's (Intel SDM
//! vol. 3A ch. 4, AMD64 APM vol. 2 ch. 5); the hook's contract is
//! wolf-lang spec/04 `[abi.target.none.alloc]` and wolf_rt_none's own
//! documentation. No Linux source; no other kernel's or libc's source.

use frames
use log
use paging
use panic
use sync

/// The heap's PML4 slot.
pub const SLOT: u64 = 384
const META: u64 = 0xffffc00000000000 // the state page, and the slot's first address
const SLOT_END: u64 = 0xffffc08000000000 // slot 385's first address
const DESC: u64 = 0xffffc00000001000 // descriptor i at DESC + 64 i
/// The first heap page's address.
pub const BASE: u64 = 0xffffc04000000000 // heap page i at BASE + 4096 i
const PAGE: u64 = 4096
const DESC_BYTES: u64 = 64
const DESC_PER_PAGE: u64 = 64 // PAGE / DESC_BYTES
const MAX_PAGES: u64 = 32768 // 128 MiB, both zones together
const CLASS_ZONE: u64 = 0x1000000 // the class zone's first page index: BASE + 64 GiB
const NIL: u64 = 0xffffffffffffffff // no page
const SMALL_MAX: u64 = 2048
const MIN_BLOCK: u64 = 16
const CLASSES: u64 = 8 // 16, 32, ..., 2048

// A descriptor's words (byte offsets).
const D_KIND: u64 = 0
const D_LEN: u64 = 8 // FREE_HEAD, LARGE: pages; FREE_TAIL: the head; SMALL: the block size
const D_NEXT: u64 = 16 // FREE_HEAD: the next free run's head, or NIL
const D_PREV: u64 = 24 // FREE_HEAD: the previous free run's head, or NIL
const D_LIVE: u64 = 24 // SMALL: allocated blocks in the page
const D_MAP: u64 = 32 // SMALL: the allocated map, four words (256 blocks of 16)

// Descriptor kinds. Every page of a free run is FREE_*, so a free of
// any page-aligned address in one is a double free; INNER is a page of
// a large block other than its first.
const INNER: u64 = 0
const FREE_HEAD: u64 = 1
const FREE_TAIL: u64 = 2
const LARGE: u64 = 3
const SMALL: u64 = 4
const FREE_INNER: u64 = 5

/// The heap's books, at the start of its state page (META), each field
/// read and written as a `u64` at its `offset_of` (as kernel/frames'
/// FrameState): module state is read only inside `unsafe`
/// ([mem.static], E1301), and a `#[repr(c)]` header in memory the heap
/// owns keeps one unsafe site, `rd`/`wr`.
#[repr(c)]
struct HeapState {
    class16: u64, // the eight class lists' heads (a block's address, 0 = empty) ...
    class32: u64,
    class64: u64,
    class128: u64,
    class256: u64,
    class512: u64,
    class1024: u64,
    class2048: u64, // ... in class order
    top: u64, // heap pages mapped: [0, top)
    desc_pages: u64, // descriptor pages mapped
    free_runs: u64, // the first free run's head, or NIL
    live_n: u64, // blocks handed out and not freed
    live_b: u64, // their bytes, as asked
    allocs_n: u64,
    frees_n: u64,
    table_n: u64, // page-table frames paging.map took for the heap
    class_top: u64, // class-zone pages mapped: [CLASS_ZONE, CLASS_ZONE + class_top)
    class_desc_pages: u64, // the class zone's descriptor pages mapped
    frames_n: u64, // every frame the heap took from kernel/frames: its pages, its books, their tables
}

/// Whether `start` has mapped the state page; the module's one `var`.
var up: bool = false

/// Whether `start` has run (the heap's one module `var`; tests/mpx2-heap
/// H10 reads it on either side of `start`, a wolf-lang#598 witness).
pub fn is_up() -> bool {
    // # Safety: a read of the module's own `var`, written once by
    // `start`; one CPU (see "No lock").
    unsafe { up }
}

// --- raw words ---------------------------------------------------------------

/// The 64-bit word at `a` in the heap's own memory.
fn rd(a: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: `a` lies in a page this module mapped (the state page,
    // a descriptor page, a heap page below `top`), 8-aligned.
    unsafe { *(a as *u64) }
}

/// Write the 64-bit word at `a`.
fn wr(a: u64, v: u64) {
    // # Safety: as `rd`.
    unsafe {
        let p = a as *u64
        *p = v
    }
}

fn desc(i: u64) -> u64 {
    DESC + i * DESC_BYTES
}

fn kind(i: u64) -> u64 {
    rd(desc(i) + D_KIND)
}

fn page_va(i: u64) -> u64 {
    BASE + i * PAGE
}

/// The class list head of class `c` (0 = 16 bytes ... 7 = 2048), in the
/// state page.
fn class_head(c: u64) -> u64 {
    rd(META + offset_of(HeapState, class16) as u64 + c * 8)
}

fn set_class_head(c: u64, v: u64) {
    wr(META + offset_of(HeapState, class16) as u64 + c * 8, v)
}

/// The books' field at byte offset `off` (an `offset_of(HeapState, …)`).
fn get(off: int) -> u64 {
    rd(META + off as u64)
}

fn set(off: int, v: u64) {
    wr(META + off as u64, v)
}

fn top() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, top))
}

// --- mapping -----------------------------------------------------------------

fn live_pml4() -> u64 {
    let c = paging.cr3()
    c - c % PAGE
}

/// Map one fresh frame at `va`, read-write no-execute. `false` when
/// `frames` is empty.
fn map_fresh(va: u64) -> bool {
    let pa = frames.alloc() else 0
    if pa == 0 {
        return false
    }
    let n = paging.map(live_pml4(), va, pa, paging.NX | paging.RW) else 99
    if n == 99 {
        panic.fail("heap: paging refused a heap page at", va)
        return false
    }
    set(offset_of(HeapState, table_n), get(offset_of(HeapState, table_n)) + n)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, frames_n), get(offset_of(HeapState, frames_n)) + 1 + n)
    true
}

/// Zero the page at `va`.
fn zero_page(va: u64) {
    var a = va
    while a < va + PAGE {
        wr(a, 0)
        a += 8
    }
}

fn oom(size: u64) {
    panic.fail("heap: out of memory, asked", size)
}

/// Map `k` more heap pages at `top` (and the descriptor pages they
/// need), and give them to the page layer as one free run.
fn grow(k: u64, size: u64) {
    if top() + get(offset_of(HeapState, class_top)) + k > MAX_PAGES {
        oom(size)
        return
    }
    while get(offset_of(HeapState, desc_pages)) * DESC_PER_PAGE < top() + k {
        let va = DESC + get(offset_of(HeapState, desc_pages)) * PAGE
        if !map_fresh(va) {
            oom(size)
            return
        }
        zero_page(va)
        set(offset_of(HeapState, desc_pages), get(offset_of(HeapState, desc_pages)) + 1)
    }
    let first = top()
    var i: u64 = 0
    while i < k {
        let t = top()
        if !map_fresh(page_va(t)) {
            oom(size)
            return
        }
        wr(desc(t) + D_KIND, INNER)
        set(offset_of(HeapState, top), t + 1)
        i += 1
    }
    release_run(first, k)
}

// --- the page layer ----------------------------------------------------------

/// Put the run [h, h + n) on the free list, tagged, in address order
/// (the list is kept sorted by head, so first-fit takes the lowest run
/// that fits and the same sequence of asks lands in the same places
/// every time the heap is empty again; a LIFO list grew the heap by a
/// page in round 2, px06's measurement).
fn push_run(h: u64, n: u64) {
    wr(desc(h) + D_KIND, FREE_HEAD)
    wr(desc(h) + D_LEN, n)
    var prev = NIL
    var next = get(offset_of(HeapState, free_runs))
    while next != NIL && next < h {
        prev = next
        next = rd(desc(next) + D_NEXT)
    }
    wr(desc(h) + D_PREV, prev)
    wr(desc(h) + D_NEXT, next)
    if prev == NIL {
        set(offset_of(HeapState, free_runs), h)
    } else {
        wr(desc(prev) + D_NEXT, h)
    }
    if next != NIL {
        wr(desc(next) + D_PREV, h)
    }
    if n > 1 {
        wr(desc(h + n - 1) + D_KIND, FREE_TAIL)
        wr(desc(h + n - 1) + D_LEN, h)
    }
}

/// Take the free run headed at `h` off the free list (its pages'
/// kinds are the caller's to rewrite).
fn unlink_run(h: u64) {
    let next = rd(desc(h) + D_NEXT)
    let prev = rd(desc(h) + D_PREV)
    if prev == NIL {
        set(offset_of(HeapState, free_runs), next)
    } else {
        wr(desc(prev) + D_NEXT, next)
    }
    if next != NIL {
        wr(desc(next) + D_PREV, prev)
    }
}

fn is_free(k: u64) -> bool {
    k == FREE_HEAD || k == FREE_TAIL || k == FREE_INNER
}

/// Give the run [h, h + n) back to the page layer, merged with a free
/// run on either side.
fn release_run(h: u64, n: u64) {
    var head = h
    var len = n
    var i: u64 = 0
    while i < n {
        wr(desc(h + i) + D_KIND, FREE_INNER)
        i += 1
    }
    // The run after: free when its first page is a FREE_HEAD.
    let after = h + n
    if after < top() && kind(after) == FREE_HEAD {
        let an = rd(desc(after) + D_LEN)
        unlink_run(after)
        wr(desc(after) + D_KIND, FREE_INNER)
        len += an
    }
    // The run before: its last page is a FREE_TAIL (naming its head) or
    // a one-page FREE_HEAD.
    if h > 0 {
        let k = kind(h - 1)
        var bh = NIL
        if k == FREE_TAIL {
            bh = rd(desc(h - 1) + D_LEN)
        } else if k == FREE_HEAD {
            bh = h - 1
        }
        if bh != NIL {
            let bn = rd(desc(bh) + D_LEN)
            unlink_run(bh)
            wr(desc(h - 1) + D_KIND, FREE_INNER)
            head = bh
            len += bn
        }
    }
    push_run(head, len)
}

/// The first free run of at least `n` pages, or NIL.
fn first_fit(n: u64) -> u64 {
    var h = get(offset_of(HeapState, free_runs))
    while h != NIL {
        if rd(desc(h) + D_LEN) >= n {
            return h
        }
        h = rd(desc(h) + D_NEXT)
    }
    NIL
}

/// `n` contiguous heap pages: the first page's index. Grows the heap
/// when no free run fits (out of memory panics).
fn take_pages(n: u64, size: u64) -> u64 {
    var h = first_fit(n)
    if h == NIL {
        // A free run ending at `top` is extended, not stranded.
        var have: u64 = 0
        let t = top()
        if t > 0 {
            let k = kind(t - 1)
            if k == FREE_TAIL {
                have = rd(desc(rd(desc(t - 1) + D_LEN)) + D_LEN)
            } else if k == FREE_HEAD {
                have = 1
            }
        }
        grow(n - have, size)
        h = first_fit(n)
        if h == NIL {
            panic.fail("heap: no run after growing, pages", n)
            return 0
        }
    }
    let len = rd(desc(h) + D_LEN)
    unlink_run(h)
    if len > n {
        push_run(h + n, len - n)
    }
    var i: u64 = 0
    while i < n {
        wr(desc(h + i) + D_KIND, INNER)
        i += 1
    }
    h
}

/// One fresh page for a size class, from the class zone: mapped at
/// the zone's bump (with its descriptor page as needed), never
/// returned. Class pages live apart from the run layer so they never
/// split a run: with no large block live, the run layer is one free
/// run again, and the next round's asks land where the last round's
/// did (px06: class pages taken from the run layer grew the heap by a
/// page in round 2).
fn take_class_page(size: u64) -> u64 {
    let ct = get(offset_of(HeapState, class_top))
    if top() + ct + 1 > MAX_PAGES {
        oom(size)
        return 0
    }
    let i = CLASS_ZONE + ct
    let dp = get(offset_of(HeapState, class_desc_pages))
    if dp * DESC_PER_PAGE < ct + 1 {
        let va = DESC + CLASS_ZONE * DESC_BYTES + dp * PAGE
        if !map_fresh(va) {
            oom(size)
            return 0
        }
        zero_page(va)
        set(offset_of(HeapState, class_desc_pages), dp + 1)
    }
    if !map_fresh(page_va(i)) {
        oom(size)
        return 0
    }
    set(offset_of(HeapState, class_top), ct + 1)
    i
}

// --- the block layer ---------------------------------------------------------

/// The class of a small block of `size` bytes at `align`: 0 for 16 ...
/// 7 for 2048; CLASSES when it is not small.
fn class_of(size: u64, align: u64) -> u64 {
    var need = size
    if align > need {
        need = align
    }
    var c: u64 = 0
    var b = MIN_BLOCK
    while c < CLASSES {
        if need <= b {
            return c
        }
        b = b * 2
        c += 1
    }
    CLASSES
}

fn class_bytes(c: u64) -> u64 {
    MIN_BLOCK << c
}

/// Bit `k` of a small page's allocated map.
fn map_bit(i: u64, k: u64) -> bool {
    (rd(desc(i) + D_MAP + k / 64 * 8) >> (k % 64)) & 1 == 1
}

fn flip_map_bit(i: u64, k: u64) {
    let a = desc(i) + D_MAP + k / 64 * 8
    let one: u64 = 1
    wr(a, rd(a) ^ (one << (k % 64)))
}

/// A fresh page for class `c`, its blocks threaded on the class list
/// in address order.
fn carve(c: u64, size: u64) {
    let i = take_class_page(size)
    let bs = class_bytes(c)
    wr(desc(i) + D_KIND, SMALL)
    wr(desc(i) + D_LEN, bs)
    wr(desc(i) + D_LIVE, 0)
    var w: u64 = 0
    while w < 4 {
        wr(desc(i) + D_MAP + w * 8, 0)
        w += 1
    }
    let va = page_va(i)
    var a = va + PAGE - bs
    var next = class_head(c)
    while a >= va && a < va + PAGE {
        wr(a, next)
        next = a
        if a == va {
            a = 0
        } else {
            a -= bs
        }
    }
    set_class_head(c, next)
}

fn alloc_small(c: u64, size: u64) -> u64 {
    if class_head(c) == 0 {
        carve(c, size)
    }
    let a = class_head(c)
    set_class_head(c, rd(a))
    let i = (a - BASE) / PAGE
    let k = (a - page_va(i)) / class_bytes(c)
    flip_map_bit(i, k)
    wr(desc(i) + D_LIVE, rd(desc(i) + D_LIVE) + 1)
    a
}

fn free_small(i: u64, p: u64, size: u64, align: u64) {
    let bs = rd(desc(i) + D_LEN)
    let c = class_of(size, align)
    if c == CLASSES || class_bytes(c) != bs {
        panic.fail("heap: free with the wrong size, asked", size)
        return
    }
    let off = p - page_va(i)
    if off % bs != 0 {
        panic.fail("heap: free of an address inside a block", p)
        return
    }
    let k = off / bs
    if !map_bit(i, k) {
        panic.fail("heap: double free", p)
        return
    }
    flip_map_bit(i, k)
    wr(desc(i) + D_LIVE, rd(desc(i) + D_LIVE) - 1)
    wr(p, class_head(c))
    set_class_head(c, p)
}

fn pages_of(size: u64) -> u64 {
    (size + PAGE - 1) / PAGE
}

fn free_large(i: u64, p: u64, size: u64) {
    if p % PAGE != 0 {
        panic.fail("heap: free of an address inside a block", p)
        return
    }
    let n = rd(desc(i) + D_LEN)
    if pages_of(size) != n {
        panic.fail("heap: free with the wrong size, asked", size)
        return
    }
    release_run(i, n)
}

// --- the interface -----------------------------------------------------------

/// Bring the heap up: map and zero its state page. Needs `frames`
/// started and PAX's own paging live (`paging.start`). Panics by name
/// when `frames` cannot give the state page.
pub fn start() {
    let before = frames.free_count()
    if !map_fresh(META) {
        oom(PAGE)
        return
    }
    zero_page(META) // the books start at zero: count the state page's own frames again
    let taken = before - frames.free_count()
    set(offset_of(HeapState, table_n), taken - 1)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, frames_n), taken)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, free_runs), NIL)
    // # Safety: the module's own `var`, written once, here.
    unsafe {
        up = true
    }
}

/// `size` bytes at a multiple of `align` (a power of two, at most 4096):
/// the address. Never 0; out of memory panics. Not zeroed.
pub fn alloc(size: u64, align: u64) -> u64 {
    let s = sync.acquire(sync.heap())
    let a = alloc_locked(size, align)
    sync.release(sync.heap(), s)
    a
}

fn alloc_locked(size: u64, align: u64) -> u64 {
    if !is_up() {
        panic.fail("heap: alloc before heap.start, asked", size)
        return 0
    }
    if size == 0 || size > 0x7fffffffffffffff {
        panic.fail("heap: alloc of a size that is not positive", size)
        return 0
    }
    if align == 0 || align & (align - 1) != 0 || align > PAGE {
        panic.fail("heap: alloc with a bad alignment", align)
        return 0
    }
    var a: u64 = 0
    let c = class_of(size, align)
    if c < CLASSES {
        a = alloc_small(c, size)
    } else {
        if size > MAX_PAGES * PAGE {
            oom(size)
            return 0
        }
        let i = take_pages(pages_of(size), size)
        wr(desc(i) + D_KIND, LARGE)
        wr(desc(i) + D_LEN, pages_of(size))
        a = page_va(i)
    }
    set(offset_of(HeapState, live_n), get(offset_of(HeapState, live_n)) + 1)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, live_b), get(offset_of(HeapState, live_b)) + size)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, allocs_n), get(offset_of(HeapState, allocs_n)) + 1)
    a
}

/// Give back the block at `p`, allocated with `size` and `align`.
/// Panics by name on a double free, an address outside the heap or
/// inside a block, and a size that is not the block's.
pub fn free(p: u64, size: u64, align: u64) {
    let s = sync.acquire(sync.heap())
    free_locked(p, size, align)
    sync.release(sync.heap(), s)
}

fn free_locked(p: u64, size: u64, align: u64) {
    if !is_up() || !in_zones(p) {
        panic.fail("heap: free outside the heap", p)
        return
    }
    let i = (p - BASE) / PAGE
    let k = kind(i)
    if k == SMALL {
        free_small(i, p, size, align)
    } else if k == LARGE {
        free_large(i, p, size)
    } else if is_free(k) && p % PAGE == 0 {
        panic.fail("heap: double free", p)
        return
    } else {
        panic.fail("heap: free of an address no block starts at", p)
        return
    }
    set(offset_of(HeapState, live_n), get(offset_of(HeapState, live_n)) - 1)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, live_b), get(offset_of(HeapState, live_b)) - size)
    set(offset_of(HeapState, frees_n), get(offset_of(HeapState, frees_n)) + 1)
}

/// Whether `p` lies in a mapped heap page of either zone.
fn in_zones(p: u64) -> bool {
    let runs = p >= BASE && p < page_va(top())
    let cz = page_va(CLASS_ZONE)
    runs || (p >= cz && p < cz + get(offset_of(HeapState, class_top)) * PAGE)
}

/// Whether `va` lies in the heap's slot (its books or its pages). A
/// range, not `va >> 39 == …`: the release tier deletes a branch on the
/// top half of a `u64 >> k` (wolf-lang#600), and a caller's `if` on this
/// would be one once inlined.
pub fn contains(va: u64) -> bool {
    va >= META && va < SLOT_END
}

/// Heap pages mapped, both zones (the high-water mark: the heap never
/// shrinks).
pub fn pages() -> u64 {
    if is_up() { top() + get(offset_of(HeapState, class_top)) } else { 0 }
}

/// Pages mapped in the class zone.
pub fn class_pages() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, class_top))
}

/// Descriptor pages mapped, and the state page: the heap's books.
pub fn book_pages() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, desc_pages)) + get(offset_of(HeapState, class_desc_pages)) + 1
}

/// Every frame the heap has taken from kernel/frames (its pages, its
/// books and the page tables mapping them); it never gives one back.
pub fn frames_taken() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, frames_n))
}

/// Page-table frames `paging.map` took for the heap's slot.
pub fn table_frames() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, table_n))
}

/// Blocks handed out and not yet freed.
pub fn live_blocks() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, live_n))
}

/// Their bytes, as asked.
pub fn live_bytes() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, live_b))
}

pub fn allocs() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, allocs_n))
}

pub fn frees() -> u64 {
    get(offset_of(HeapState, frees_n))
}

/// Free page runs, and the pages in them.
pub fn free_pages() -> u64 {
    var n: u64 = 0
    var h = get(offset_of(HeapState, free_runs))
    while h != NIL {
        n += rd(desc(h) + D_LEN)
        h = rd(desc(h) + D_NEXT)
    }
    n
}

/// `heap: slot 384 at 0x<base>, P pages, C class pages, Q free, B live
/// blocks, Y live bytes, A allocs, F frees, M book pages, T table
/// frames, N frames taken` (P counts both zones; Q is the run layer's
/// free pages; N = P + M + T).
pub fn report() {
    log.put("heap: slot ")
    log.dec(SLOT as int)
    log.put(" at ")
    log.hex(BASE)
    log.put(", ")
    log.dec(pages() as int)
    log.put(" pages, ")
    log.dec(class_pages() as int)
    log.put(" class pages, ")
    log.dec(free_pages() as int)
    log.put(" free, ")
    log.dec(live_blocks() as int)
    log.put(" live blocks, ")
    log.dec(live_bytes() as int)
    log.put(" live bytes, ")
    log.dec(allocs() as int)
    log.put(" allocs, ")
    log.dec(frees() as int)
    log.put(" frees, ")
    log.dec(book_pages() as int)
    log.put(" book pages, ")
    log.dec(table_frames() as int)
    log.put(" table frames, ")
    log.dec(frames_taken() as int)
    log.put(" frames taken")
    log.end()
}

// --- wolf's allocator hook (kw12, [abi.target.none.hooks] (d)) -------------

/// The freestanding runtime's allocation: `size` bytes at `align`.
export fn wolf_alloc(size: i64, align: i64) -> *u8 {
    if size <= 0 || align <= 0 {
        panic.fail("heap: wolf_alloc of a size that is not positive", size as u64)
    }
    let a = alloc(size as u64, align as u64)
    // # Safety: an address in the heap's mapped pages, `size` bytes long.
    unsafe { a as *u8 }
}

/// The freestanding runtime's free: the block at `p`, with its own size
/// and alignment.
export fn wolf_free(p: *u8, size: i64, align: i64) {
    // # Safety: the pointer's address only; nothing is read through it.
    let a = unsafe { p as u64 }
    free(a, size as u64, align as u64)
}
